Used my daggers and retreats cagily at the beginning, found a few
graves early (mediocre mid-level stuff mostly).  Had some vicious pets
between levels 12 and the castle (Titan, Mastodons (ridden), Rock
Trolls), but stopped maintaining them after the Valley of the Dead. 
Never collected gems in this game.  I think freeing up unnecessary
concerns (pets, gems) gives you fewer things to think about during the
game.

One thing that I think helped is I turned the keyboard repeat rate
down on my keyboard... allowed you to walk and rest more safely.  Give
it a try.  (I play the win32 version on Windows ME [but I just
compiled it on Solaris 2.8, so give me a little slack ;)]

Finally had all the good things I needed for the endgame/Astral Plane
by the time I got there.  First non-spellcaster I've ever taken to the
Astral Plane.  Never saw a magic lamp in the whole game.  Didn't worry
about (or achieve) any voluntary challenges.  Two of the wishes it
credited me with were whiffs (Unfortunately, nothing happens), or at
least I think those got counted.

I've been playing this game since '93.  I ascended a priest once with
a cheatsave file I used once, and killed an archaeologist and a
tourist (most recently) on the astral plane.

